00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.460
To all the regulars.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.429
Round 7 of the giveaway starts now.

00:00:23.429 --> 00:00:25.949
Remember all you have to do to participate
is be a subscriber and leave a comment on

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:26.949
this video.

00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:27.949
I’ll just pick someone at random.

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:31.769
This episode made me so happy, so let’s
do top 5 moments and then my review.

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:35.690
Time to Fly, Careful for spoilers from the
episode if you haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:36.720
Here we got.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.180
Number 5 - The Hound explains why he and Arya
are the same.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:45.750
It was both heartbreaking and adorable watching
the Hound lick his wounds like a real dog.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.930
But then he just breaks down emotionally in
front of Arya.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:53.680
She had just done her big nothing is nothing
dark jedi in training speech so seeing her

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.940
be so genuine with him seemed a little strange.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.500
I love the two of them together, they push
all the right fandom buttons.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.330
But if she were really turning into a stone
cold killer, she wouldn’t feel sentiment

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.800
for the Hound.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.210
She wouldn’t have offered to treat his wound.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.039
Fire or no fire.

00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:13.530
In case you didn’t remember, we learned
the Hounds story about the Mountain burning

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.330
his face during the tournament where they
fought.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.130
Way way back when everyone was still alive.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.189
I think someone was explaining it to Sansa.

00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:26.920
I’m surprised given their similar family
upbringing that the Hound and Tyrion never

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.149
became friends.

00:01:28.149 --> 00:01:37.179
Tyrion learned to deal with all the hate by
being witty, but it seems like the Hound just

00:01:37.179 --> 00:01:46.159
turned everything inward and it became this
festering psychological wound.

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:48.570
Number 4 - Melisandre and Selyse

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.210
How surprised were you that Melisandre just
copped to perpetrating a lot of bullshit.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:56.439
It seemed like 99 percent of her vials were
full of tricks.

00:01:56.439 --> 00:01:58.649
But there was that one, the one you don’t
want to touch.

00:01:58.649 --> 00:01:59.889
So it’s not all BS.

00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:01.310
I wonder what’s in that one.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:06.299
Also, we can’t escape that scene without
staring at the black hole that was her boobs.

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:09.789
I enjoy nudity on game of thrones as much
as the next pervert.

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:13.320
But were you surprised at how long the camera
lingered on her in the tub.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.960
It’s like Melisandre was forcing Seylse
to look at her naked.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.480
Like she has power over all flesh.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.690
It’s hard to tell if Melisandre was trolling
her or not.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:26.610
Because she dropped a huge bomb.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:31.930
Remember how last season she talked about
the power in royal blood and the Gendry escaped.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:35.300
I think they might be changing things from
the books and taking Shireen with them because

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.940
Melisandre wants to use her for something.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.950
It’s not something that happens in the books.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.970
But I’m really really curious to see where
they take that sub plot.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.700
So don’t forget about Shireen, she just
got way more important.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.080
Number 3 - Podrick and Brienne enjoy some
Hot Pie

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.290
I love Hot Pie so much, I’m so glad they
brought him back this early.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:57.620
I actually just thought they were making a
subtle reference to Harrenhaal in season 2

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:02.600
and the Brotherhood in season 3 but they went
full on and he spilled his hot pie guts about

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:03.600
Arya.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.210
You can tell he must be starved for conversation.

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:09.660
Or maybe he just talks that much with all
his customers.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:15.160
I like the idea of a chatty Hot Pie baking
direwolf bread just enjoying his simple life

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.690
away from all the intrigue.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:19.400
Like he’s the only character on the show
that gets a happy ending.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.150
That would be hilarious.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.100
But this whole situation was a huge win for
Podrick, because he’s the one that did the

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.540
Math and figured out the Hound would be taking
Arya to the Eyrie.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.070
When they were at the crossroads, did anyone
else think that bandits would jump out and

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.540
stab them?

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:37.230
Anytime things get too quiet and characters
start looking around like they’re lost I

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.960
expect a sword to just materialize inside
their guts.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:43.730
This is what happens when you watch too much
Game of Thrones.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:48.800
Number 2 - Oberyn agrees to be Tyrion’s
Champion

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.570
The way they acted out that scene and the
music cues they used made it feel like a huge

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:53.960
battle had been won.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.980
Like the end of episode 5 when Ghost came
back to Jon and you could just hear the whole

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.000
world cheering at the same time.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.900
I loved Oberyn story about visiting Tyrion
at Casterly Rock when he was young.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.390
That’s actually from the books.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.230
One of several book moments in the episode.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:13.140
There was even the shout out from when Cersei
almost yanked off Tyrion’s dick.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.380
I wince every time I read that part.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.660
Wow she’s horrible.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.590
When is her reckoning coming?

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:23.699
If you didn’t see, Oberyn was actually crying
a little when he was talking about using Tyrion’s

00:04:23.699 --> 00:04:26.120
trial to begin his quest for Justice.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.400
The Mountain is just the first person on the
list.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.419
It sounds like he plans on killing a lot of
people.

00:04:31.419 --> 00:04:32.539
Not just Lannisters.

00:04:32.539 --> 00:04:38.120
I appreciate the level of detail they went
to with how Cersei described Tyrion being

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.120
a monster.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.449
Claws, Tail and a giant head.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:50.999
and my number 1 WTF moment - Littlefinger
makes Lysa Fly

00:04:50.999 --> 00:04:56.270
All of the Eyrie Sansa scenes were straight
out of the book, from the Snow Castle of Winterfell,

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.370
to the Littlefinger kiss to the Moon Door.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:02.749
They really sped that plot up too, because
it’s from book 4 and back in King’s Landing

00:05:02.749 --> 00:05:04.479
the trail is a book 3 thing.

00:05:04.479 --> 00:05:09.949
I totally don’t mind, as creepy as Littlefinger
was with Sansa he gets a lot of the best speeches.

00:05:09.949 --> 00:05:13.500
That should actually be a contest, see who
gives the best speech each season on Game

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.289
of Thrones.

00:05:16.289 --> 00:05:18.440
Sansa is getting in deeper and deeper with
Littlefinger.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:22.350
She had no idea what was going on with the
Purple Wedding plot, but this time she had

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:25.610
ringside seats for Lysa’s Murder.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:27.510
And she is a really terrible liar.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:31.710
Plus they have to deal with King Robyn.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:36.860
As long as Littlefinger can keep the other
lords of the vale from taking over his stewardship,

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.100
Sansa will probably be okay.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.560
Because Robyn is very Joffrey-Like in his
mood swings.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.379
And the Moon Door is always going to be a
threat hanging over everyone’s head.

00:05:44.379 --> 00:05:46.360
It’s like the ultimate prison sentence.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:50.259
Like the Arryn’s can just push all their
problems into a nice little circular death

00:05:50.259 --> 00:05:51.259
hole.

00:05:51.259 --> 00:05:54.050
But now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite moment was.

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:56.069
And to all the book readers out there.

00:05:56.069 --> 00:06:02.189
How do you feel about Arya being so nice to
the Hound?

00:06:02.189 --> 00:06:04.849
That’s one change from the books that I’m
actually pretty happy about.

00:06:04.849 --> 00:06:09.710
It seems like they’re making his character
much bigger than he was in the books, just

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:11.550
because those two work so well together on
screen.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.970
Just so we don’t forget about Daenerys or
anything else going on, here’s a couple

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.270
things to keep track of.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:20.729
First off, Daenerys is sending Daario to subdue
all the Wise Masters in Yunkai.

00:06:20.729 --> 00:06:22.949
I loved that he was so restless.

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:26.699
He actually does have desires beyond Daenerys,
but yeah.

00:06:26.699 --> 00:06:30.559
That look on her face made me laugh so hard.

00:06:30.559 --> 00:06:34.849
Daario was already confirmed for season 5,
so he’s not going to die or anything.

00:06:34.849 --> 00:06:37.400
But we’ll have to wait and see what happens
with the Wise Masters.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:43.220
Then the other big thing is the defense of
Castle Black.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:46.370
Alliser Thorne pretty much ignores Jon Snow’s
warning.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:50.849
He and Sam are basically going to sit on top
of the Wall until that Wildling Raiding party

00:06:50.849 --> 00:06:51.880
comes within eye shot.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.479
But they will be able to see them coming.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:56.259
So at least Jon will get that “I told you
so” moment.

00:06:56.259 --> 00:06:59.169
Remember, Castle Black isn’t fortified from
the South.

00:06:59.169 --> 00:07:02.099
I explained why in my bonus video from earlier
today.

00:07:02.099 --> 00:07:05.319
I’ll have a link to that in the description
if you want to learn more about it.

00:07:05.319 --> 00:07:07.750
Overall the episode was actually pretty happy.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:13.880
I gave it an A minus just because I’m trying
to reserve A’s and A pluses for the best

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.620
one or two episodes of all ten this season.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:20.189
It was really an episode of strong character
moments, yes Lysa flying through the Moon

00:07:20.189 --> 00:07:22.219
Door was mostly a shocking moment.

00:07:22.219 --> 00:07:24.940
But the rest of the episode was surprisingly
positive.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:29.039
I couldn’t feel better about the Hound and
Arya, it’s like a few episodes ago she thought

00:07:29.039 --> 00:07:33.330
he was the worst human being on the planet,
and now she’s taking care of him.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:37.069
Even Jaime and Tyrion were acting like they
were little brothers trying to play a prank

00:07:37.069 --> 00:07:38.069
on their dad.

00:07:38.069 --> 00:07:41.360
Like they were two little boys just trying
to get a rise out of Tywin.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.530
That look they shared, it was like they were
remembering their entire childhood.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:49.259
I always love the way the show mixes these
really strong character moments with the oh

00:07:49.259 --> 00:07:51.150
shit Moon Door scenes.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:54.870
Even Littlefinger’s speech to Sansa was
really touching, about getting revenge for

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.479
Catelyn and the Red Wedding.

00:07:56.479 --> 00:08:00.270
He kind of took back all that good will when
he kissed Sansa in that creepy way.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.300
But for a minute his heart was in the right
place.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:06.430
Let me know if there’s any big moments that
you think I left out.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:11.080
Actually I just remember Lolly’s, it’s
funny and a bit dark when you remember what

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.270
happened to her that led to marrying her off
to Bronn.

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:15.619
Also remember, there’s no new episode next
week.

00:08:15.619 --> 00:08:16.990
So I’ll be posting a bonus video instead.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.370
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:20.439
My Q&amp;A video will post tomorrow like normal.

00:08:20.439 --> 00:08:22.560
Right now you can click here to get it.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.389
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post
it.

00:08:24.389 --> 00:08:26.360
